A narrow beam of electrons, all with the same speed, is incident normally on a carbon film. The electrons then move on to a fluorescent screen, as illustrated in Fig. 9.1.

{{figure:figure_9_1}}

The apparatus is in a vacuum.
The pattern produced on the screen is shown in Fig. 9.2.

{{figure:figure_9_2}}

